@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title DELETE /api/workspace/v1/messenger/stream_bindings/[binding_uuid]
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceStreamBindingController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Background performers\nexact scope leases + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: DELETE /api/workspace/v1/messenger/stream_bindings/{binding_uuid}
API -> DB: lock persistent USER_STREAM_BINDING\nactive=false; membership_generation++
API -> DB: immutable outbox event For each typed task
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: topic_membership_policy_rebuild / read_counters /\nfolder_projection / delivery_snapshot_event\neach task It has its own outbox_event_uuid
Worker -> Worker: topic scope: Hide it placement access;\nuser-stream/user-folder: shared projections
Worker -> DB: conditional by active=false + new generation;\nstale generation = no-op
Worker -> Projection: remaining access bindings/containers
Worker -> Events: event to delete the stream/bind/folder\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over API,Worker
  After commit All of them . message/reaction paths They demand active membership
  and generation equality; cleanup The old ones . rows No , not really . security boundary.
  Task lifecycle: lease expiry/fencing, retry/backoff, DLQ/reaper.
end note
@enduml
